    "taxonId": 70054,
    "summary": "An annual trailing vine whose modern cultivated form originated in Sudan. Its large fruit has a firm rind and sweet, juicy flesh, usually deep red or pink, though other colours and seedless varieties occur. The flesh is eaten raw or pickled, while the rind is edible after cooking.",
    "humanEdibility": "yes",
    "edibilityNote": "The fruit is eaten raw, pickled or as juice; the rind is cooked, and the seeds may be roasted or ground into flour.",
